::kind(api)

::meta{crate: tomet-transform, dependencies: list(tomet-ast, tomet-expr, tomet-parser, tomet-search, tomet-semantics, tomet-style, tomet-tree), dependents: list(tomet-js, tomet-load, tomet-tests, tomet-vault, tomet-workspace)}

=[tomet-transform]

Pure in-memory AST refactoring and structural transformations for Tomet documents.

Provides:

- (expressions) Every `${...}` in a document resolved once, in one pass, with the
evaluator's typed values put back according to where each expression sits.
- (macro_rewrite) Reverse URL-to-macro pattern matching and rewriting.
- (directive) Directive promotion (`::meta.type` -> `::kind`) and Value DSL normalization.
- (structural) Structural AST query matching and in-place transformations (rename tag, rename key, replace value).
- (meta) Batch `::meta` key/value updates.

==[Module blueprint]

Blueprint schema extraction, transformation, and instantiation.

===[Structs]

====[struct BlueprintInfo]

Metadata and variable definitions extracted from a `::blueprint` directive.

====[struct Instantiated]

What [`instantiate_blueprint`] did.

===[Functions]

====[fn extract_blueprint_info]

Extracts [`BlueprintInfo`] from `doc` if it declares a top-level `::blueprint` directive.

====[fn instantiate_blueprint]

Instantiates a blueprint `doc` in-place by:
1. Promoting/converting `::blueprint(target)` to `::kind(target)` and stripping schema blocks.
2. Resolving every `${...}` in it, with `cx` -- which is a creating context
(`Phase::Create`), the only place `generate.*` and `vars` exist.

==[Module directive]

Directive promotion and Value DSL normalization transformations.

===[Functions]

====[fn promote_prop_to_directive]

Promotes a property `prop_key` from an element matching `source_filter` into a new top-level
declaration `::target_directive_name(val)` (or `::target_directive_name{...}`), inserting it at `target_index`
(or automatically after any `::version` directive, or at position 0).

If the property is absent, empty, or null, it is simply removed without creating a directive.
Returns `true` if a directive was created and inserted.

====[fn promote_meta_type_to_kind]

Promotes `::meta`'s `type:` field to a top-level `::kind(...)` element.

==[Module expressions]

Resolving every `${...}` in a document, once, before anything renders it.

This is the single place where an expression's value is put back into a
document. It replaces three passes that each handled some positions: the
body (`interp`), the arguments of elements (`macro_expand`, called by one
binding only) and the index queries (`index_query`). What a value does at
a position is one table, in `tmtroot/spec/expressions/overview.expr.tmt`;
in short:

- data (arguments, properties): any value that can be data is kept;
- inside a paragraph: a scalar is text, a fragment of one paragraph is

spliced in, anything else is a mismatch;

- on a line of its own: a scalar is a paragraph, a fragment is its blocks;
- as a list item: a list gives one item per element, a scalar gives one;
- a document, an element, a directory, a function or a datetime has no

place in output at all.

===[A value that does not fit]

Nothing is dropped and nothing is fatal. An expression that cannot be
evaluated, or whose value has no place at its position, is written back
as its own source (`${...}`) and reported in the returned [`Unresolved`]
list, so `tomet check` can warn about it. That keeps a document that
shows `${...}` as an example working, and still gives a typo somewhere
to surface.

===[What an expression sees]

The caller's [`EvalContext`] decides: which phase, which documents, which
macros. References resolve through its resolver, so a caller that wants
them answered from the document @strong[as written] -- and it should -- hands
in a resolver that returns the document from before this pass rewrote it.

===[Structs]

====[struct Unresolved]

Something the pass left as it found it, and says so.

===[Enums]

====[enum UnresolvedKind]

What an [`Unresolved`] is about.

===[Functions]

====[fn resolve_expressions]

Replaces every `${...}` in `doc` with what it stands for.

==[Module links]

===[Enums]

====[enum TargetMode]

Destination target format when rewriting `ref:` links and `@embed` assets.

===[Functions]

====[fn resolve_document_links]

Walks `doc` and resolves any `ref:` targets and local `@embed` targets using `resolver`.

- Resolved links have their target rewritten according to `mode`.
- Unresolved links are rewritten to the `unresolved:` scheme (e.g. `unresolved:Note Name`).

==[Module macro_rewrite]

Reverse URL-to-macro pattern matching and rewriting.

===[Structs]

====[struct MacroPattern]

A compiled macro matcher for reverse URL-to-macro rewriting.

====[struct MacroSet]

A collection of macro patterns sorted by specificity (longer constant prefix first).

===[Functions]

====[fn transform_link_targets_with_macros]

Transforms link targets in `doc` matching any macro in `macro_set` into `$macro(...)` invocations.

==[Module meta]

Metadata element manipulation in documents.

===[Functions]

====[fn set_meta_in_doc]

Updates or inserts a key-value pair in a target directive/metadata block (e.g. `::meta`).
If the target block is not found, prepends a new directive block at position 0.

==[Module structural]

Structural in-place AST transformations.

===[Enums]

====[enum StructuralAction]

===[Functions]

====[fn apply_structural_action]

Applies a structural refactoring action to all matching elements in `doc`.
Returns the number of transformations applied.
